[{"id":"VRCE-5-53-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":1,"english":"Beholding Lankā burnt down and devastated and the demons terrified, the monkey Hanumān began to reflect.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.757,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"171c42b61b1eca315c61f30059e2c4714a4e9f5024b969d29479bdee00dc0e0f","compact":"7850d5b7bb5fa0e13ba81b00b35a09b4e4f0b8590052b6cbef665f9082f583dd","nasal":"6066672bc31397d1a8e132646e17a62919ab93be95e96581ad8281cd7472996c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":2,"english":"And worked up with fear and remorse, he reflected, “What a mighty iniquity have I perpetrated by burning down Lankā of my own accord.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"da3aeff1988f1515a46823fa5fbf7f097563408ffab6896fb65f4a3b5163d22d","compact":"d40f8027528f3878527cdf52c630c418825beb80e3a0be06d2bd71446f522a41","nasal":"a4fda3772c9165e2c198b4ea00db5025bdd10a7fe2b54a2f767079071c56742c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":3,"english":"Blessed are those high-souled ones who control their wrath by dint of their own good sense, like to fire quenched by water.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.747,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3c5126840955190d27bd04406541ab3d371cdeaef74a8d4baebcad7aee0e2e7e","compact":"194437ccc48812be63ba43541c370cde2f07adda766b012da23ba91fa3993a8e","nasal":"3188aa62f27889836e4c77e4600604c148479c4511df7d51ee30c2d36fce1a5e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":4,"english":"Forsooth has the worshipful Jảnaki been burnt, since the whole city of Lankā has been devastated with fire. And she being burnt, foolishly have I spoilt the work of my master.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.817,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"54af725c00ad8e4df313c6b84f8f1b1dfda86896a76b55ac3e7ee1cb5c08de8a","compact":"5580bdb5d248bfd6340fefac28e48468c048cf39b39ac664f40476fc59cd81a1","nasal":"91ca9aa90bd0a46d9342a9055e127f67d7a1d422b2c4af00e46b44e9a571fd7f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":5,"english":"I have defeated the great object for which I have laboured so much. In burning down Lankā, I have not saved Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8d3c95b70fd320cc377ade4115f0956d3b2a72e7da7d27bd30b9559a7a8094a7","compact":"bf0196028228c23f85a33d40931cb82b895a121ac0d1b2673206cad79975a002","nasal":"b2005a319b045465a25c627d110a4c57b3c92509390372bb393de925601401f3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":6,"english":"To have burnt down Lankā is assuredly a trifle, but in my ire I have lost my great object. Forsooth has Janaki been consumed, since I behold no spot in Lankā which is not made desolate with fire-in fact the whole city has been reduced to ashes.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a8e90aeeb553e961b6034ad293fddeb92fbc4fc600d2d946df497134e97a2039","compact":"4943e6f50e5c952ce68a12e2c34b8a9eb6dc6c3e0a4843a5a173ce5b0c1f7416","nasal":"604e5b27830235c81af2dbccbf66ae8d80cdff2289eab44ffb1884a90bde26df"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":7,"english":"To have burnt down Lankā is assuredly a trifle, but in my ire I have lost my great object. Forsooth has Janaki been consumed, since I behold no spot in Lankā which is not made desolate with fire-in fact the whole city has been reduced to ashes.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"adb94e4e0edcfb06ba10068469a41aaf933eccdadd59778c46057fa04b297e0d","compact":"2772b6e1a2a3063e6cecc8d7ab93455fc30c07f4cce5036879a1e584c2760da9","nasal":"7e8cab77c90185384d21f4c118287aa9c221554964d72a66cdc25430019c3a72"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":8,"english":"As I have committed such an injury under the influence of my perverse understanding, it behave me to relinquish my life here.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.887,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"82c2a618cff60d33dc8695a6d0427d72c91e48febe4274fc0da94ab688e4647f","compact":"c99fc1cd2d8556a6bb74bb0eb153d3b369807ad8a3287b4fa8f6bc9caa08bb69","nasal":"c99fc1cd2d8556a6bb74bb0eb153d3b369807ad8a3287b4fa8f6bc9caa08bb69"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":9,"english":"I shall jump into this flame or into a submarine fire, or I shall resign my mortal frame to the animals that infest the ocean.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0cec6aa5f7420a04961c0f194e77ea16252f96dddc70fb04c25c29a4bf2f1439","compact":"1ca8392cafd2d9ed102b25a4a9f827ed8205a7faa784b5f4b076cb935fe8a494","nasal":"1ca8392cafd2d9ed102b25a4a9f827ed8205a7faa784b5f4b076cb935fe8a494"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":10,"english":"For, living, I shall not be able to face that lord of monkeys, and how shall I, having spoilt their work utterly, show myself to those foremost of men?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.919,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"62682238110ed8ffeaf6a1689ad9f6106a72a971a15e5ac72266bc2ac0ecd60d","compact":"73f47be6023d265497bdd12acf9198809dd16eda92c06adc0325983bef0687f1","nasal":"73f47be6023d265497bdd12acf9198809dd16eda92c06adc0325983bef0687f1"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":11,"english":"I have through my culpable passion furnished an illustration of the reckless monkey-nature, which is well known over the three worlds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e7e0c784e51284c4efc6e34f6e4a0cf485fcfd5149527d82fd8f1a877abe0663","compact":"d1a492e2b5df8a911b527747036fc7f0d6c77ed06f356c9fa8e3c55ce54ce5ab","nasal":"216ec333d996c080913587320d66e7eacdb176b8eac71f5a4e6da1d731954f20"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":12,"english":"Fie on this activity, born of (the quality of) passion, which is the source of incompetence and rashness; since although capable, I did not protect Sita.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bcf4ddc1aebe75762248d4c955eaf01c637842273128384c09c26535b6321d0e","compact":"952f5a56c3f1abe7aa9155888c5c7ec18a8d9c5845927140333b5fb53c3e4000","nasal":"952f5a56c3f1abe7aa9155888c5c7ec18a8d9c5845927140333b5fb53c3e4000"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":13,"english":"On Sītā having met with destruction, both of them (Rāma and Lakşmaņa) shall cease to exist; and on their ceasing to exist, Sugrīva shall die along with his friends.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1c0e66980cbafbf246cd601d25aec74a05d2cbfa82c3d70479b67f60444c434a","compact":"be67659993b105976e7d76a741a45787675e57f37d55a63557ba94bc66902d43","nasal":"cdb22c15183b4bed52b5a4de06df7567c8b84d3950ca9e8a25f11b5aaf608905"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":14,"english":"Hearing these tidings, how shall the righteous Bharata, attached to his brother (Rāma), along with Satrughna, live?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2e7eea15356cb7e882eca30f039eb222cf0eb32aacd4e2a5cd4b26016f2c4f2e","compact":"0a4e4f25edbc5096fabda622359b764694b4e043eaa11969e97e891b4d65b1ad","nasal":"0a4e4f25edbc5096fabda622359b764694b4e043eaa11969e97e891b4d65b1ad"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":15,"english":"And on the virtuous Ikşvāku race being extinct, without doubt, all the subjects shall be overwhelmed with grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a8581e06ceb3db4ba86d4797d6afb45ab31efc47c3e5a9409ef4b55bb9c6b804","compact":"d3a3a3d4cb18d34b45a884e7fea5bc552bad7666fde0529b8592821a887465a6","nasal":"b0e4259f95c24f73362e429c831912ac2cef5e3eb48571a7ff0eda79d83d3cde"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":16,"english":"Therefore, I of crust luck has had my harvest of virtue and profit taken away; and being under the influence of baleful passion, I am the cause of the destruction of creatures.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"71b629a8db90411f58dab48dc460e900f64140b79e746727559ae459667518eb","compact":"09c9639f07b1e520bc125e19493e2d0c55d66e46af6abbaa51756ec40212015b","nasal":"09c9639f07b1e520bc125e19493e2d0c55d66e46af6abbaa51756ec40212015b"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-17","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":17,"english":"As he was reflecting thus, he bethought him of auspicious omens which he had witnessed since.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.891,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"387f37fa888a796fa59db2146bf616783d83b01806e4ead533144347e4b9e7e4","compact":"fd119ec7e77afb242738e4817b526a552c04904afef0969240333d21ef55c36d","nasal":"080bb18980550f17e876382615d6e2c70145003c4daab914972b985b928ab88a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-18","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":18,"english":"Or it may be that one of charming limbs has been preserved by her proper energy. The blessed one may not have met with her end, for fire dose burn fire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053018","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0cd4c6d57c5059996387b589bc43519d0fd54a2ae373023fae30a0294315d9a6","compact":"90ccb3218a8789c473dfae79e983171545dcde16a20f688050eb61c2fef14977","nasal":"8390f706023506a13715e44454a248f5654f642ca28e47162328b9fafa470e96"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-19","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":19,"english":"Fire should not touch the spouse of that virtuous one of immeasurable energy, who is protected by her own character.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.768,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053019","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b772cd834fb5a755f38b7ca6065da1b1e278b776b6afb1ca8ad2234f42cda0f8","compact":"63e2da9060a7887c1c22b28951a432cb58d5e28a63e2f4bda6fce0e647414c0c","nasal":"63e2da9060a7887c1c22b28951a432cb58d5e28a63e2f4bda6fce0e647414c0c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-20","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":20,"english":"And that bearer of sacrificial offerings has not burnt me, is owing to Rāma's power and the virtue of Vaidehi.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"91f7152a843d1313971d291fa6523a7d3fbb7498f62f8da2b8a15b419ba39375","compact":"8ecd009242d15eedb0f618e160da3bc17b0db62c0b6bc01552ddd4772d46ecae","nasal":"8ecd009242d15eedb0f618e160da3bc17b0db62c0b6bc01552ddd4772d46ecae"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-21","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":21,"english":"Why should she that is a very goddess to the three brothers, Bharata and the others, and that has enchanted the mind of Rāma, meet with destruction?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.724,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5ff121958815c9a6269de6830814c7233cc3c57fb186f5fc2f90caa0a07753f8","compact":"a20b8ba09b903342e9fe66c969e13fd8706748952014b8b929fe1be921f14b4d","nasal":"47e734f1d0e16e7ab527a6071b5c41a576e47e31da4100a01caa55de48df39ce"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-22","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":22,"english":"When that everywhere unspent Lord, having burning for his office, has not consumed my tail, why should he burn the exalted lady?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053022","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b70fae2227ae2c479b8c441ddce39da4ac616d29a4d7431a7088bda8300a6540","compact":"261a45c20c3c37a5855a840f902dbd0042878d47869bc7752ab45f041c2eff59","nasal":"ed3f275e3e2177d2830c822e4f17b2d1000454c32bcce4ca15234574c1c08282"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-23","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":23,"english":"By virtue of her asceticism, veracity, and devotion to her lord she it is that can consume Fire, but Fire cannot burn her.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.703,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053023","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"39cd45687a3a3ae34d1977b790de2a4fd622e22edf493ae5a253a92c05b294a5","compact":"d8affbe4aa243583467a0ad3ede978218d65cbc64da541641321e597d3e01fc5","nasal":"d8affbe4aa243583467a0ad3ede978218d65cbc64da541641321e597d3e01fc5"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-24","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":24,"english":"And as Hanumān was thinking of the magnitude of that revered lady's religious merit, he heard the converse there of high-souled Caranas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.776,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053024","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ea631823fd760fafe5ef623bb4f537b61cc8aa2d95a20efcfe17d023a682e686","compact":"6607ec16c04c9f2d3f6687249b2792d68f73ab184afc88a9a9f092346adaf247","nasal":"d503b15e3f261f6e8ede2d9e2f996916cf8ab361339601817629ebd22d9f9c66"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-25","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":25,"english":"Ah! hard is the feat that Hanumān has forsooth achieved. He has created a terrific and fierce conflagration in the abode of the Rākşasa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.557,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053025","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a4c43480f4e6804846bc73739cbf94784b40fc3f509eaaf03ec62e869ab6f460","compact":"67d57d9b840e4b54443f64b8b8b0fbcdbdba7c6b0b7131e05bcce535b1258b0e","nasal":"67d57d9b840e4b54443f64b8b8b0fbcdbdba7c6b0b7131e05bcce535b1258b0e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-26","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":26,"english":"The females of Rākşasa accompanied by boys and old folks, are flying amain; and in consequence of the hubbub it seems as if (Lankā) is in lamentation through her mountaincaverns. Burnt is this city of Lankā with her turrets, walls and gate-ways; and we are astonished that Jānakī is not burnt.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053026","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4677f7444842d89fcb642232520dc40c93239b15ffc0ca13e8f07a30c72b703f","compact":"f970e7b415450637678d612e26c8d04e71d1fb6ab0cfc6cc17b1e4e696fae86d","nasal":"d05d858040b5a482fd7116bfa21ac87a5afc12ede467e361a8325ca6c14da29a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-27","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":27,"english":"And what through the auspicious omens that he had witnessed, and what through the speech of the saints, Hanumān was delighted (beyond measure).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053027","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"67abcc32cf27c5f5233ca9dbdd1342dbef768d4df4ee4799e229cc4334c9ee4f","compact":"021e4b604a65f5d7b51150a4e798ef6f2b948f7e0f8a5fc81407201b6fe8e73e","nasal":"021e4b604a65f5d7b51150a4e798ef6f2b948f7e0f8a5fc81407201b6fe8e73e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-53-28","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":53,"verse":28,"english":"Then the monkey, with his end attained, knowing that the king's daughter was unhurt, became bent upon returning after seeing her once again.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.914,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-55-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5053028","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a6dadfa4494338c35bed5505ab5200a60706c5f77cb215d13f660d7d85ec3598","compact":"f704db8d0d8d22ed251ad675